"""Publish native gallery evidence without altering earlier trials."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib
import json
import shutil
import markdown

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]
HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
RUN = ROOT / 'ada_run/encounter_pilot/Random_Entropy/hybrid-gallery'
for name in ['report.json', 'hall-gallery.png', 'hall-gallery-replayed.png', 'source_manifest.json']:
    shutil.copy2(RUN / name, HERE / ('museum-report.json' if name == 'report.json' else name))
reports = [json.loads((HERE / name).read_text(encoding='utf8')) for name in ['verification.json', 'museum-report.json']]
assert all(report['passed'] for report in reports)
counts = [len(report['checks']) for report in reports]
wall = json.loads((ROOT / 'commons/maps/Random_Entropy/writing_wall.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
assert wall['order'][:6] == ['shannon_entropy_meter', 'entropy_jar', 'entropy_compartments', 'entropy_axiom', 'entropy_ruin', 'signal_room']
style = '''body{margin:0;background:#f1eee5;color:#233b39;font:18px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1440px;margin:auto;padding:24px}h1{font:clamp(32px,4vw,50px)/1.1 Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0 16px}h2{font:29px Georgia,serif}p{max-width:85ch}small{letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5d736c}a{color:#166965}nav{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}section{margin:30px 0}figure{margin:0}img{display:block;width:100%;max-height:78vh;object-fit:contain;background:#101d25}figcaption{padding:12px;background:#e0e5d9}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}.grid img{max-height:none}code{font-size:.9em}td,th{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #aebfb3}table{border-collapse:collapse}pre{overflow:auto}.steps{padding:18px 28px;background:#e0e5d9}li{margin:8px 0}@media(max-width:850px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}'''
page = f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>A gallery of kept hybrids · Ada Research</title><style>{style}</style><main>
<header><small>Ada Research / Random_Entropy / 16 October 2026</small><h1>A gallery of kept hybrids</h1><p>KEEP several arrangements while exploring seeds. GALLERY places four saved sets side by side, with their seed and slider stage. Replay any entry to return to its exact form at full size.</p><nav><a href="#try">Try it in the room</a><a href="#replay">A kept moment, restored</a><a href="guide.html">Reconstruction guide</a><a href="#evidence">Verification</a></nav></header>
<section><figure><img src="gallery-close.png" alt="Native Godot gallery: four saved arrangements labelled seeds 435, 436, 437 and 438; seed 437 is saved at stage 0.73"><figcaption>Native Godot capture. Each tray holds one complete saved set of four forms. The third entry keeps an intermediate stage, 0.73. Five entries were kept in this trial; the fifth is on the next page.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="try" class="steps"><h2>Keep, compare, return</h2><ol><li>At the prefab experiment near the Entropy hall entrance, select <strong>HYBRIDS</strong>.</li><li>Press <strong>SEED +1</strong> to explore. Press <strong>KEEP</strong> whenever an arrangement is worth revisiting. Each press adds an entry.</li><li>Open <strong>GALLERY</strong>. Compare four kept sets at once. <strong>PREVIOUS / NEXT</strong> browse additional pages.</li><li>Select <strong>REPLAY 1–4</strong> for the corresponding entry. Its saved seed, stage and exact part poses return to the main experiment.</li><li><strong>BACK</strong> leaves the live arrangement unchanged. Reopening the scene retains the collection.</li></ol><p>The standalone <code>commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder/preview.tscn</code> has matching desktop controls. These web images document the native instrument; the buttons operate inside Godot.</p></section>
<section id="replay"><h2>A kept moment, restored</h2><div class="grid"><figure><img src="gallery-four.png" alt="Four saved sets in the gallery"><figcaption>Four entries side by side. Seed 437 was kept while its parts were still recombining.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="gallery-replayed.png" alt="Seed 437 restored to stage 0.73 in the full-size experiment"><figcaption>REPLAY 3 restores seed 437 at 0.73, including every saved part pose.</figcaption></figure></div><p>Compare seeds at the same stage first. Follow one recognisable part: what does it carry now, or what carries it? If a relationship suggests a new use, replay that entry at full size before deciding what made it interesting. Gallery miniatures are fitted uniformly to their trays; the saved experiment is unchanged.</p></section>
<section><h2>Installed in the Entropy hall</h2><figure><img src="hall-gallery.png" alt="Kept hybrid gallery in the actual Entropy hall"><figcaption>The room probe opens GALLERY through its physical button, checks four complete saved sets, and replays the oldest entry.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="evidence"><h2>What the checks establish</h2><p><strong>{counts[0]} apparatus checks and {counts[1]} actual-hall checks pass.</strong> They cover exact miniature/source poses, five distinct saves, multiple pages, an intermediate stage, older-entry replay, reopening a fresh scene, previous-save migration and unavailable files. Inactive consoles stop receiving collisions. The existing seeded assembly and reversible slider checks also pass.</p><p>Each KEEP file remains complete. A local gallery index links the records; more saves add pages instead of replacing earlier entries. Missing or incompatible records show UNAVAILABLE. An unreadable index is preserved. The previous latest KEEP joins the gallery on first use after the upgrade.</p><p>The tests establish retention and replay. Whether a form is compelling, recognisable or suggestive of a new use still needs a person's observation. Headset comfort remains untested.</p><nav><a href="verification.json">Apparatus checks</a><a href="museum-report.json">Room checks</a><a href="gallery-records.json">Five complete saved records</a><a href="manifest.json">Source fingerprints</a><a href="../2026-10-16-seeded-hybrids/index.html">Seeded assembly trial</a></nav></section></main></html>'''
(HERE / 'index.html').write_text(page, encoding='utf8')
guide = (ROOT / 'commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder/README.md').read_text(encoding='utf8')
(HERE / 'implementation.md').write_text(guide, encoding='utf8')
guide = guide.replace('../../../doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-hybrid-gallery/README.md', 'index.html')
(HERE / 'guide.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Kept gallery reconstruction</title><style>' + style + '</style><main><a href="index.html">← Kept gallery</a>' + markdown.markdown(guide, extensions=['tables', 'fenced_code']) + '</main></html>', encoding='utf8')
paths = list((ROOT / 'commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder').glob('*.gd')) + list((ROOT / 'commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder').glob('*.tscn'))
paths += [ROOT / 'commons/artifacts/registry/prefab_disorder.json']
paths += [ROOT / 'commons/maps/Random_Entropy' / name for name in ['map_data.json', 'writing_wall.json', 'tutorial.md', 'final.md', 'artifacts.md']]
for source in ['cardboard_box', 'computer_monitor', 'lab_stool', 'microscope']:
    paths += [ROOT / 'commons/artifacts' / source / (source + suffix) for suffix in ['.gd', '.tscn']]
(HERE / 'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checks': counts, 'gallery_schema': 'prefab-hybrid-gallery/1', 'record_schema': 'prefab-disorder/2', 'visible_entries': 4, 'main_order': wall['order'][:6], 'sha256': {p.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix(): hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in paths}}, indent=2), encoding='utf8')
(HERE / 'README.md').write_text(f'''# Gallery of kept hybrids

16 October 2026. User asks to keep several interesting hybrids with their seeds, compare them side by side and replay any one.

[Native gallery](index.html) · [Implementation guide](implementation.md) · [Apparatus checks](verification.json) · [Actual hall checks](museum-report.json) · [Five complete records](gallery-records.json) · [Source manifest](manifest.json).

KEEP adds a complete arrangement to a persistent local index. Each entry holds all four forms and fifty meshes, with seed and slider stage. GALLERY shows four uniformly fitted sets at a time. PREVIOUS/NEXT navigate additional pages; REPLAY 1–4 restores the selected full-size arrangement; BACK preserves the live experiment. Main REPLAY returns to the most recently selected/kept entry during the session. After reopening, main REPLAY reads the latest KEEP pointer and GALLERY still offers all entries. Older records are not evicted.

`gallery_store.gd` manages the index and migrates the previous latest pointer. `kept_gallery.gd` reads validated records, builds only the visible page, and routes selection through the existing replay path. The pose calculation is shared with the host, so miniature previews use the same stored draws and targets. Missing/incompatible records become UNAVAILABLE. An unreadable index is retained without being overwritten. Native hidden consoles have their processing and collision layers disabled.

{counts[0]}/{counts[0]} apparatus checks and {counts[1]}/{counts[1]} actual-hall checks pass. The tests keep five distinct variants, include stage 0.73, compare all miniature transforms with their records, page to a fifth entry, restore older entries, reopen a fresh instance, verify migration and malformed/missing-file behavior, and press the installed physical controls. Existing generator, slider reversal and earlier-record checks also pass. Test pointers are isolated from the user's collection. The malformed-index fixture is intentional; JSON parsing returns failure without emitting a misleading runtime error.

Reproduce with `python -X utf8 doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-hybrid-gallery/run.py`, then `python -X utf8 tools/run_encounter_probe.py Random_Entropy --sequence randomness --render --no-bridges --output-tag hybrid-gallery --probe doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-hybrid-gallery/museum_probe.gd`. Run `publish.py` here after both pass.

The optional tutorial, writing-wall entry, registry and research card/plan describe the gallery. Main room/final order and the first 48-value pilot remain in place. Next human observation: compare two seeds at the same stage, follow one identifiable part and record why a relationship is worth keeping. Recognition, learner reconstruction and headset comfort remain untested. The separate matched-base-motion refinement is still proposed; this gallery does not resolve that confound.
''', encoding='utf8')
print('Published', HERE / 'index.html', counts)
